          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Beyond price, these are the reasons families choose Voxblock as a Toniebox alternative.</p><h3>Simple, physical interaction</h3><p>Where the Toniebox uses figurines placed on top of the device, Voxblock uses solid blocks that slot into the player. Each block is a different <a href=\"/collections/audiobooks\">audiobook</a>, so children choose by the artwork on the front and feel in control of what they hear.</p><h3>No wi-fi required</h3><p>Voxblock works completely offline and right out of the box. There is no wi-fi setup and nothing to download, which suits travelling and homes with unreliable internet.</p><h3>Durable for active use</h3><p>The blocks are sturdy and built to be handled repeatedly by little hands. The player is portable, so it goes to the park, on a road trip or to a friend’s house.</p><h3>Long battery life</h3><p>The player runs for up to 16 hours on a charge by USB-C, so it rarely runs out in the middle of a story.</p><h3>Calm, independent listening</h3><p>With no screens and no connectivity to manage, children can focus on the story and choose for themselves. Suitable for <a href=\"/collections/audiobooks?filter.p.m.book.age_groups=Under+5%27s\">younger children</a> and older listeners alike.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
